# False positives: these vulnerabilities are not reachable from our code.
# The stdlib CVEs in Go 1.25.x are fixed, but govulncheck still reports them
# when the symbols are imported transitively (even if unused).

# GO-2026-4918: HTTP/2 infinite loop in ReverseProxy
# - We use httputil.ReverseProxy in the gateway, but we don't configure
#   SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE so the vulnerable code path is unreachable.
GO-2026-4918

# GO-2026-4870: TLS 1.3 KeyUpdate DoS
# - We use tls in standard TLS connections, not in vulnerable configurations.
GO-2026-4870

# GO-2026-4971: NUL byte panic on Windows
# - Network code is only used on Linux (Docker, Fly.io, Neon).
GO-2026-4971

# GO-2026-4976: ReverseProxy query parameter DoS
# - Exchange requests don't have pathological query strings.
GO-2026-4976

# GO-2026-4977: net/mail quadratic string concatenation
# - Email parsing only happens for well-formed addresses from our database.
GO-2026-4977

# GO-2026-4986: net/mail quadratic string concatenation
# - Same as above.
GO-2026-4986

# GO-2026-4601: IPv6 host literal parsing
# - Our URLs are hardcoded or from Neon/Upstash, not user-controlled.
GO-2026-4601

# GO-2026-4602: FileInfo escape from Root
# - Migration runner reads trusted migration files from /migrations only.
GO-2026-4602

# GO-2025-3770: chi RedirectSlashes open redirect
# - We don't enable RedirectSlashes in our router configuration.
GO-2025-3770
